      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Three Records of Truth\nA `helm_release` leaves three records:\n\n1. The Terraform state holds the inputs: the\nchart, its version and its values.\n2. Helm keeps its own record of each release,\nwith the rendered objects, in a Secret in the\ncluster.\n3. The live objects run in the cluster.\n\nA `helm upgrade` or a `kubectl edit` outside\nTerraform changes the second or the third\nrecord, but not the first. So the plan can say\n\"No changes\" while the cluster differs from\nthe code ([issue 372](https://github.com/hashi\ncorp/terraform-provider-helm/issues/372)). The\nhelm provider has an option that stores the\nrendered objects in the state, so a plan can\ncompare them ([manifest experiment](https://gi\nthub.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-helm/blo\nb/v3.3.0/docs/index.md#L201-L213)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-98d144a708e5",
      "originalText": "Three Records of Truth\nA `helm_release` leaves three records:\n\n1. The Terraform state holds the inputs: the chart, its version and its values.\n2. Helm keeps its own record of each release, with the rendered objects, in a Secret in the cluster.\n3. The live objects run in the cluster.\n\nA `helm upgrade` or a `kubectl edit` outside Terraform changes the second or the third record, but not the first. So the plan can say \"No changes\" while the cluster differs from the code ([issue 372](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-helm/issues/372)). The helm provider has an option that stores the rendered objects in the state, so a plan can compare them ([manifest experiment](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-helm/blob/v3.3.0/docs/index.md#L201-L213)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "three-records-of-truth"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
