      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Every Field Has One Owner\nKubernetes records which client set each field\nof an object. With server-side apply, it\nreports a conflict when a second client tries\nto set the same field ([server-side apply](htt\nps://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/using-api/se\nrver-side-apply/)). Controllers also set\nfields after Terraform creates an object. For\nexample, the AWS Load Balancer Controller sets\nthe class of a Service that asks for a load\nbalancer. A diff that comes back after every\napply means two owners write one field.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-e55d6da0359e",
      "originalText": "Every Field Has One Owner\nKubernetes records which client set each field of an object. With server-side apply, it reports a conflict when a second client tries to set the same field ([server-side apply](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/using-api/server-side-apply/)). Controllers also set fields after Terraform creates an object. For example, the AWS Load Balancer Controller sets the class of a Service that asks for a load balancer. A diff that comes back after every apply means two owners write one field.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "every-field-has-one-owner"
      }
    },
