      "text": "CRDs Have Their Own Lifecycle\nA custom resource definition adds a new kind\nto the cluster's API, such as `PrometheusRule`\nor `ExternalSecret`. A chart can bring its\nCRDs in a `crds` folder. Helm installs that\nfolder once and never upgrades or deletes it:\n\"There is no support at this time for\nupgrading or deleting CRDs using Helm\" ([Helm\nCRD guide](https://github.com/helm/helm-www/bl\nob/d869ccd3db838b63cee08bffb8400e1a9221c3ee/ve\nrsioned_docs/version-3/chart_best_practices/cu\nstom_resource_definitions.md#L30-L45)). A\ncustom resource, an object of such a kind, can\nonly exist after its CRD exists. That creates\nan order between charts, and between charts\nand the resources that use their kinds.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-b00d113fcb0b",
      "originalText": "CRDs Have Their Own Lifecycle\nA custom resource definition adds a new kind to the cluster's API, such as `PrometheusRule` or `ExternalSecret`. A chart can bring its CRDs in a `crds` folder. Helm installs that folder once and never upgrades or deletes it: \"There is no support at this time for upgrading or deleting CRDs using Helm\" ([Helm CRD guide](https://github.com/helm/helm-www/blob/d869ccd3db838b63cee08bffb8400e1a9221c3ee/versioned_docs/version-3/chart_best_practices/custom_resource_definitions.md#L30-L45)). A custom resource, an object of such a kind, can only exist after its CRD exists. That creates an order between charts, and between charts and the resources that use their kinds.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "crds-have-their-own-lifecycle"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
