    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8546201118,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-90da9994fb46",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1321.2,
      "y": 1680.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 612.5,
      "seed": 468424,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What You Will See\n| Resource | What it is | What to check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `aws_eks_cluster` | the control plane |\nKubernetes version, access mode, endpoint\naccess |\n| `aws_eks_node_group` | a group of worker\nmachines | Machine image source, sizes,\nignored fields |\n| `aws_eks_addon` | an EKS add-on, such as the\nnetwork plugin | Pinned version per Kubernetes\nversion |\n| `aws_eks_access_entry` | IAM principal\nmapped to Kubernetes access | Who gets cluster\nadmin |\n| `helm_release` | one installed chart |\n`version`, values source, `wait`, `atomic`,\n`timeout` |\n| `kubernetes_deployment`,\n`kubernetes_config_map`, and other typed\nresources | one object of a known kind |\nNamespace, labels, restarts on config change |\n| `kubernetes_manifest` | any object,\nincluding custom resources | The CRD it needs\nat plan time |\n| `kubectl_manifest` | raw YAML, from a\ncommunity provider | Which fork, and\nserver-side apply |\n| `kubernetes_secret` | a Secret | Its data\nsits in the state in plain text |\n\nA chart can also be configured from a template\nfile with `templatefile`, which renders the\nvalues from variables. The rendered values\nthen appear in the plan as one block of text.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-90da9994fb46",
      "originalText": "What You Will See\n| Resource | What it is | What to check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `aws_eks_cluster` | the control plane | Kubernetes version, access mode, endpoint access |\n| `aws_eks_node_group` | a group of worker machines | Machine image source, sizes, ignored fields |\n| `aws_eks_addon` | an EKS add-on, such as the network plugin | Pinned version per Kubernetes version |\n| `aws_eks_access_entry` | IAM principal mapped to Kubernetes access | Who gets cluster admin |\n| `helm_release` | one installed chart | `version`, values source, `wait`, `atomic`, `timeout` |\n| `kubernetes_deployment`, `kubernetes_config_map`, and other typed resources | one object of a known kind | Namespace, labels, restarts on config change |\n| `kubernetes_manifest` | any object, including custom resources | The CRD it needs at plan time |\n| `kubectl_manifest` | raw YAML, from a community provider | Which fork, and server-side apply |\n| `kubernetes_secret` | a Secret | Its data sits in the state in plain text |\n\nA chart can also be configured from a template file with `templatefile`, which renders the values from variables. The rendered values then appear in the plan as one block of text.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "k8s-what-you-will-see"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4380873432,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-fe71c58c37f1",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1309.2,
      "y": 1940.0,
