      "height": 227.5,
      "seed": 595333,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Controller Fields Force Replacement\nThe AWS Load Balancer Controller sets\n`spec.loadBalancerClass` when a Service of\ntype LoadBalancer is created ([controller docs\n](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/aws-load-\nbalancer-controller/blob/v3.6.3/docs/deploy/in\nstallation.md#L12-L13)). That field cannot\nchange, and the Kubernetes provider replaces\nthe Service when it differs from the code. So\nevery apply deletes and recreates the Service,\nand the load balancer gets a new address.\nWrite the field into the configuration with\nthe value that the controller sets.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-1d77f3ed09aa",
      "originalText": "Controller Fields Force Replacement\nThe AWS Load Balancer Controller sets `spec.loadBalancerClass` when a Service of type LoadBalancer is created ([controller docs](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/aws-load-balancer-controller/blob/v3.6.3/docs/deploy/installation.md#L12-L13)). That field cannot change, and the Kubernetes provider replaces the Service when it differs from the code. So every apply deletes and recreates the Service, and the load balancer gets a new address. Write the field into the configuration with the value that the controller sets.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "controller-fields-force-replacement"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
