    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2232560022,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-240a3f2575f3",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1883.1999999999998,
      "y": 4723.0,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 332.5,
      "seed": 403341,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Version Upgrades\nEKS raises the control plane one minor version\nper update, and the nodes must catch up before\nthe next step ([update a cluster](https://docs\n.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/update-cl\nuster.html)). Add-on versions belong to a\nKubernetes version, so each version change\nalso changes add-on pins. A node group that\nreads its machine image version from AWS's\n\"recommended\" parameter replaces its nodes\nwhenever AWS publishes a new image, even\nduring an unrelated change ([node group doc](h\nttps://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider\n-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/r/eks_node_grou\np.html.markdown#L69-L77)). A node replacement\ndrains pods, and it fails after 15 minutes if\npods cannot be evicted ([node updates](https:/\n/docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/mana\nged-node-update-behavior.html)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-240a3f2575f3",
      "originalText": "Version Upgrades\nEKS raises the control plane one minor version per update, and the nodes must catch up before the next step ([update a cluster](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/update-cluster.html)). Add-on versions belong to a Kubernetes version, so each version change also changes add-on pins. A node group that reads its machine image version from AWS's \"recommended\" parameter replaces its nodes whenever AWS publishes a new image, even during an unrelated change ([node group doc](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.73.0/website/docs/r/eks_node_group.html.markdown#L69-L77)). A node replacement drains pods, and it fails after 15 minutes if pods cannot be evicted ([node updates](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/managed-node-update-behavior.html)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "k8s-version-upgrades"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9683192796,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-09bcb6211502",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1871.1999999999998,
      "y": 4983.0,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "#FEF3C7",
      "width": 418.8,
      "height": 220.0,
