    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 6197784659,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-3287ace321b2",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1321.2,
      "y": 5255.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 386.40000000000003,
      "height": 157.5,
      "seed": 772129,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Split the Cluster from Its Contents\nThe Kubernetes provider recommends separate\napplies for the cluster and for what runs\ninside it. Two states give reliable plans even\nwhen the cluster is new or replaced, at the\ncost of two pipelines and a data source that\nconnects them. One state gives one plan per\nchange, at the cost of a manual bootstrap with\n`-target` steps.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-3287ace321b2",
      "originalText": "Split the Cluster from Its Contents\nThe Kubernetes provider recommends separate applies for the cluster and for what runs inside it. Two states give reliable plans even when the cluster is new or replaced, at the cost of two pipelines and a data source that connects them. One state gives one plan per change, at the cost of a manual bootstrap with `-target` steps.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "split-the-cluster"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9616412530,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-1b461f2ac71e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1309.2,
      "y": 5464.5,
